eue the same target, so the order should not matter, but no test in this package drives the summon through real IPC in a running shell and presses a key afterwards.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":865},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":948},{"id":"shell/Ui/ConfirmDialog.qml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-VJR1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: on a real Quickshell, does the next key after a summon over the confirmation reach the new prompt?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live summon over a raised uninstall confirmation\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:open"],"scenario":"with the confirmation raised on the root menu, summon the root route again (keybind pressed twice): the confirmation closes and nothing is removed; pressing Delete again raises it again"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"A second press of the menu keybind sends a route summon for the current menu. With the PR it cancels the pending confirmation like any other summon, so the user must press Delete again to uninstall. VJR1 states this for every summon; whether a maintainer wants that for a same-route summon is a product question, not a test result.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":34},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-VJR1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: is dismissing the confirmation also right when the summon re-opens the menu the user is already in?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Same-route summon over the confirmation\".","status":"needs_t